          </div>
          <div class="gallery-item">
            <img src="/images/keystrok/team.png" alt="Team management" />
            <div class="gallery-caption"
              >Team: invite members, set roles, and gate the irreversible
              actions to admins</div
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Quote Section -->
      <div class="quote-section">
        <blockquote class="large-quote">
          "I didn't want another dashboard to babysit. I wanted a tool that
          surfaces the one key that needs attention, walks me through fixing it,
          and otherwise gets out of the way."
        </blockquote>
        <cite class="quote-author">— The design thesis behind Keystrok</cite>
      </div>

      <!-- Validation Section -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-number">06 — WHAT SHIPPED</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Not a prototype. A working product.</h2>
          <p class="section-description">
            Keystrok runs today: open source, self-hostable, and doing the full
            job end to end. I designed it and built it, this is the real feature
            set, not a roadmap.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="results-grid">
          <div class="results-metrics">
            <div class="metric-item">
              <span class="metric-label"
                >Scan a GitHub repo (via a GitHub App) or a local folder for
                exposed secrets, stored hashed and masked</span
              >
              <span class="metric-value">Discovery</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric-item">
              <span class="metric-label"
                >Promote real findings to a tracked inventory, each with a
                rotation deadline from its severity</span
              >
              <span class="metric-value">Ledger</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric-item">
              <span class="metric-label"
                >Step-by-step, operator-gated walkthroughs; the revoke step is
