      <!-- Key Learnings Section -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <span class="section-number">08 — OUTCOME</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Why This Matters</h2>
          <p class="section-description">
            Keystrok is proof of how I work: I don't stop at the mockup. I
            research a real problem, make opinionated design decisions, and ship
            a working product, learning whatever engineering it takes to get
            there. That's what I bring to a senior product design role.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="problem-grid" style="margin-top: 80px;">
          <div class="problem-content">
            <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
            <p style="margin-bottom: 32px;">About Technical Product Design:</p>
            <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 24px;">
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Developers value focus over features - Do one thing
                exceptionally well</li
              >
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Visual design matters in DevTools - Good aesthetics improve
                adoption</li
              >
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Open source builds trust - Transparency is crucial for security
                tools</li
              >
            </ul>

            <p style="margin: 32px 0;">About Building While Designing:</p>
            <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 24px;">
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Implementation constraints improve design</li
              >
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Real data exposes edge cases mockups miss</li
              >
              <li style="border: none; padding: 8px 0;"
                >Community feedback is gold</li
              >
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="problem-sidebar">
            <h4 class="sidebar-title">Personal Growth</h4>
            <p class="sidebar-story" style="font-style: normal;">
              I taught myself the TypeScript, Next.js, and security engineering
              to build this for real, not just design it. Research to a shipped,
              self-hosted product, it's the most end-to-end thing I've made.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 24px; color: #18a0fb;">
              The clearest lesson: I had commercial demand in hand and chose to
              make Keystrok open source anyway. For a security tool, trust and
              transparency matter more than capture, and that was a deliberate
              product decision, not a default.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
